# SFT execution status v0.126: one-shot native coordinator failure preserved

2026-09-27. AWS login succeeded. The approved generated-only CPU rehearsal
ran once on a fresh t3.large. Preparation succeeded; import exited 1.
No retry occurred. Gate 5 is still incomplete. No real checkpoint, S3 model
data, GPU, inference or training was used. Production eligibility is false.

## Observed result

- Exact source archive v0.2 and all 34 CPU wheels staged successfully.
  The authenticated Ubuntu host ran Python 3.12.3 and systemd 255.
- Before staging, the expiry timer, worker identity, cgroup controllers,
  encrypted 20-GiB volume, pinned SSH host key and setup firewall were checked.
  Bootstrap v0.2 added a shared non-resetting 1-GiB HTTPS inbound quota and
  rejected HTTP and IPv6 HTTP(S); its three synthetic tests and Ruff passed.
  This tightened setup controls without changing the approved source bundle.
- Independent observation saw preparation exit 0, Result=success; import
  exit 1, Result=exit-code. Sampled memory maxima were 284,258,304 and
  19,898,368 bytes respectively; samples are not exhaustive peak telemetry.
- Supervisor retained `case_failed`, retry_allowed=false. Both exact cgroups
  were absent afterward. Stage mount was absent and its directory empty;
  no cleanup-failure record existed. All 49 original staged source hashes
  still matched after failure.
- Setup quota accounted 289,970,136 inbound bytes, with zero quota drops.
  This is the rule's packet accounting, not an exhaustive network invoice.

## Diagnostic limitation — do not guess the cause

The parent worker discards child stderr, and the entry/launcher reduce all
exceptions to generic errors. The bounded journal therefore does not reveal
the failing internal stage. Preparation passing is not proof that the import
mount view, cold loader or runtime admission passed. No OOM was reported by
the unit outcome, but the exact root cause is not established.

Next work should expose only fixed allowlisted stage/error codes, with local
synthetic regressions, before asking for a separately authorized fresh native
attempt. Do not change a security gate based on speculation, reuse the
consumed attempt, or claim the new entry has native qualification.

## Resource closure

Instance `i-0f81eea2dce2912f2` was confirmed terminated; its volume
`vol-0a8a30b35f6dab237` was confirmed absent. Endpoint
`eice-0a3c72d5b8fd419f2` reached delete-complete. Both newly created security
groups and the temporary AWS SSH-key registration returned successful deletion.
Existing instances were not changed. Generated VM payloads were ephemeral
and are not recoverable; the bounded aggregate failure evidence remains local.
No exact invoice cost is claimed.

Private records: `artifacts/lumi-vm-coordinator-native-attempt-v0.1/`
contains authorization, resource IDs, operator result, observer and cleanup
records. Prior evidence and frozen source bundle were preserved unchanged.
No commit or push was performed.

Remaining roadmap: qualify the generated native coordinator; complete
separate full-size host-bound admission and actual preserved-S3 4B CPU import
with independent package verification; then Gate 6 GPU smoke/save/resume and
SFT, Gate 7 evaluation, and Gate 8 serving. This failed tiny check does not
authorize any of those later actions.
